<title>UK: Amersham says main business growth in line.</title>
<headline>Amersham says main business growth in line.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Amersham International Plc said on Friday that growth at its main businesses -- healthcare and life sciences -- since the beginning of April was in line with its expectations.</p>
<p>Chairman Richard Lapthorne told the group's annual shareholder meeting that the &quot;performance of both businesses reflects the positive momentum achieved last year&quot;.  </p>
<p>Lapthorne said he expected the merger of Amersham Life Science and Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn's Inc's Pharmacia Biotech unit, announced on June 10, to be completed by the end of July.</p>
<p>Regulatory and shareholder approvals for Amersham's merger with Nycomed ASA of Norway, announced on July 1, should be completed by the end of September, he told shareholders.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
